== What was enumerated
The R39 native collector was widened to 16-bit coordinates and 32-bit polynomial
convolution. It enumerates the same fixed ordinary chart, lambda choices and
physical coefficient descent. Every accepted source point passes all five
original equations, eight registered units, exact Tate order 11 and the local
rank-two check. All deck and coefficient Frobenius images are rechecked.
The degree-7 control reproduces the complete old point export byte for byte.
The accepted cases are 420/540/2860/7540 rational points, respectively,
60/60/260/580 closed points and 6/6/26/58 deck orbits for degrees 7/9/11/13.
Four native attempts and one Lean workflow pass. Three named theorems and
one generated equation pass the audit, with zero failing or trusted declarations.
The exact complete point records are in results.json and
`runs/*/points/closed-points.txt`. All attempts, caps and exits are retained.

Degrees 9 and 11 were frozen before data. Degree 13 was added by a prospective
amendment after their outcomes, with unchanged 4 GiB / 1200 s build/run caps.
All field products agree with an independent carryless polynomial reduction;
all nonzero inverses and every quadratic inverse pass. Basis triples check
field identities; the old cubic exhaustive loop is not repeated at larger sizes.
Composite degree 9 is classified by actual tuple periods, including any
subfield contributions rather than assuming every point has degree 9.

== Corrected search priority
R13 already exhausted the ordinary degree-500 and degree-580 supports and
proved their retained mixed images vanish by full scalar-fiber averaging,
under its written modular/pairing bridge. R44's recommendation to screen them
again was stale. The sign obstruction in R44 is a second rejection mechanism.
R45 instead collects new source supports with ten distinct deck/Frobenius
classes, which avoid these immediate stabilizer cancellations.

== Formal scope and next obligations
The Lean module proves zero mixed projection from sign fixation and from
scalar two-step fixation, and proves that a nonzero projection requires both
to fail. These are conditional additive-group statements. They do not import
native arrays, formalize global geometry, or show that the new classes are
nonprincipal. Native compile and axiom-audit receipts are in results.json.

The next calculation is complete divisor evaluation and signed Picard classes
on the new supports, followed by actual target images and dependency checks.
Proper level-77 chosen-model transfer, quotient saturation, polarization,
theta descent and node187 coupled divisors remain separate obligations.
Larger residue fields on this fixed n=5 carrier are not a larger-n Koblitz
transfer. Independent scientific replay and semantic review remain pending.

